message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The minimum number of distinct abelian squares in a binary circular word"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattacharjee
    given-names: Deep
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0466-750X"
    affiliation: "Formerly, Electro-Gravitational Space Propulsion Laboratory (EGSPL), Bhubaneswar, Odisha 751030, India"
    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/literate-octo-lamp"
keywords:
  - abelian square
  - circular word
  - Parikh vector
  - combinatorics on words
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Every binary circular word of length n contains at least floor((n-1)/2)
  distinct abelian squares, and the words attaining this bound are determined.
  This settles Conjecture 0.6 of Simpson: its odd case holds, and in its even
  case the list of extremal words misses (ab)^{n/2} for n = 2 (mod 4),
  n >= 6. The proofs are formalized in Lean 4.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Solved and unsolved problems about abelian squares"
    authors:
      - family-names: Simpson
        given-names: Jamie
    year: 2018
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.04481"
    notes: "arXiv:1802.04481"
